# Cloudflare Pages routing — Bennett Studio.
#
# VERIFIED against `wrangler pages dev` (the real Pages asset pipeline), because
# the precedence here is not intuitive:
#
#   /*  /index.html  200   → real static assets WIN over this rule. A request
#                            for /marginprint serves the prerendered
#                            dist/marginprint/index.html; only genuinely
#                            unmatched paths fall through to index.html.
#
#   /*  /anything-else 200 → the rule wins over assets, and EVERY route serves
#                            that one file. Pointing the catch-all at a
#                            hand-rolled SPA shell therefore silently defeats
#                            the entire prerender. Don't.
#
# So the catch-all must stay `/index.html`. index.html is the prerendered
# landing page, which means an unmatched path is served landing markup; the
# `*` route in App.jsx renders <Landing /> to match it and then corrects the
# URL, so hydration stays clean.
#
# /api/* Pages Functions are evaluated before any of this.
/makerbooks    /maker-books    301
/*             /index.html     200
